 "2f4ca708dc7d985f": {
  "sections": [
   [
    "Step 1 · Prepare the grammar",
    [
     "A → Ac | Ab is left-recursive. With A → Aα1 | Aα2 | β1 | β2 (β1 = aA, β2 = bB):",
     "S  → A B\nA  → a A A' | b B A'\nA' → c A' | b A' | ε\nB  → b | a B",
     "Language: A always ends its non-recursive part with bB, and B = a*b, so every A contains at least two b’s; S adds at least one more b."
    ]
   ],
   [
    "a) Recursive procedures",
    [
     "void S()  { A(); B(); }\nvoid A()  { if (look == 'a') { match('a'); A(); A1(); }\n            else if (look == 'b') { match('b'); B(); A1(); }\n            else error(); }\nvoid A1() { if (look == 'c') { match('c'); A1(); }\n            else if (look == 'b') { /* b may start A' or the following B:\n                                       try A' first, backtrack if B then fails */\n                                    match('b'); A1(); }\n            /* else ε */ }\nvoid B()  { if (look == 'b') match('b');\n            else if (look == 'a') { match('a'); B(); }\n            else error(); }",
     "FIRST(A′) ∩ FOLLOW(A′) = {b}, so A′ needs backtracking on b; it is not a predictive (LL(1)) grammar."
    ]
   ],
   [
    "b) Is w = acadb parsed?",
    [
     {
      "table": {
       "head": [
        "Call",
        "Lookahead",
        "Action"
       ],
       "rows": [
        [
         "S() → A()",
         "a",
         "A → a A A′: match a"
        ],
        [
         "A()",
         "c",
         "no alternative starts with c ⇒ error"
        ]
       ]
      }
     },
     "Rejected. A after the first a must start with a or b, but the next symbol is c. Also, d is not a terminal of the grammar at all, and the string has only one b while every sentence needs at least three."
    ]
   ]
  ],
  "sources": [
   "Compiler Design Module 2 notes, p. recursive-descent section — left recursion, left factoring, procedures"
  ]
 },
