 "1b3efde152479eb8": {
  "sections": [
   [
    "Idea",
    [
     "Why backpatching: in a single pass the parser must emit a jump before it knows the address it jumps to (e.g. the exit of a loop or the start of an else-part). Such jumps are emitted with a blank target and remembered in lists (truelist, falselist, nextlist); when the target address becomes known, backpatch fills every jump in the list.",
     {
      "table": {
       "head": [
        "Production",
        "Semantic action (backpatching)"
       ],
       "rows": [
        [
         "B → E1 relop E2",
         "B.truelist = makelist(nextinstr); B.falselist = makelist(nextinstr + 1); emit('if' E1 relop E2 'goto _'); emit('goto _')"
        ],
        [
         "B → B1 || M B2",
         "backpatch(B1.falselist, M.instr); B.truelist = merge(B1.truelist, B2.truelist); B.falselist = B2.falselist"
        ],
        [
         "B → B1 && M B2",
         "backpatch(B1.truelist, M.instr); B.truelist = B2.truelist; B.falselist = merge(B1.falselist, B2.falselist)"
        ],
        [
         "B → ! B1",
         "B.truelist = B1.falselist; B.falselist = B1.truelist"
        ],
        [
         "M → ε",
         "M.instr = nextinstr"
        ],
        [
         "N → ε",
         "N.nextlist = makelist(nextinstr); emit('goto _')"
        ],
        [
         "S → if (B) M S1",
         "backpatch(B.truelist, M.instr); S.nextlist = merge(B.falselist, S1.nextlist)"
        ],
        [
         "S → if (B) M1 S1 N else M2 S2",
         "backpatch(B.truelist, M1.instr); backpatch(B.falselist, M2.instr); S.nextlist = merge(S1.nextlist, N.nextlist, S2.nextlist)"
        ],
        [
         "S → while M1 (B) M2 S1",
         "backpatch(S1.nextlist, M1.instr); backpatch(B.truelist, M2.instr); S.nextlist = B.falselist; emit('goto' M1.instr)"
        ],
        [
         "L → L1 M S",
         "backpatch(L1.nextlist, M.instr); L.nextlist = S.nextlist"
        ]
       ]
      },
      "caption": "makelist(i) creates a list holding instruction i; merge joins lists; backpatch(p, i) writes i as the target of every jump in list p."
     }
    ]
   ],
   [
    "Three-address code with resolved jumps (starting at 100)",
    [
     "(100) i = 0\n(101) t1 = n - 1\n(102) if i < t1 goto (104)\n(103) goto (131)\n(104) j = 0\n(105) t2 = n - i\n(106) t3 = t2 - 1\n(107) if j < t3 goto (109)\n(108) goto (128)\n(109) t4 = j * 4\n(110) t5 = arr[t4]\n(111) t6 = j + 1\n(112) t7 = t6 * 4\n(113) t8 = arr[t7]\n(114) if t5 > t8 goto (116)\n(115) goto (125)\n(116) t9 = j * 4\n(117) temp = arr[t9]\n(118) t10 = j + 1\n(119) t11 = t10 * 4\n(120) t12 = arr[t11]\n(121) arr[t9] = t12\n(122) t13 = j + 1\n(123) t14 = t13 * 4\n(124) arr[t14] = temp\n(125) t15 = j + 1\n(126) j = t15\n(127) goto (105)\n(128) t16 = i + 1\n(129) i = t16\n(130) goto (101)",
     "Note: the source’s inner loop header for (i = 0; j < n−i−1; i++) is read as for (j = 0; j < n−i−1; j++)."
    ]
   ],
   [
    "How backpatching resolved each forward jump",
    [
     {
      "table": {
       "head": [
        "Jump",
        "Kept in",
        "Filled when",
        "Target"
       ],
       "rows": [
        [
         "103 goto _ (i < n−1 false)",
         "outer B.falselist",
         "after the whole outer loop",
         "131"
        ],
        [
         "108 goto _ (j < n−i−1 false)",
         "inner B.falselist",
         "start of the outer increment i++ is reached",
         "128"
        ],
        [
         "115 goto _ (arr[j] > arr[j+1] false)",
         "if B.falselist → S.nextlist",
         "start of the inner increment j++ is reached",
         "125"
        ],
        [
         "102 / 107 / 114 if … goto _ (true exits)",
         "truelists",
         "immediately at the next M (body start)",
         "104 / 109 / 116"
        ],
        [
         "127 goto 105, 130 goto 101",
         "—",
         "emitted with known targets (loop tests already generated)",
         "105, 101"
        ]
       ]
      }
     }
    ]
   ]
  ],
  "sources": [
   "Compiler Design Module 4 notes, p. backpatching section — truelist / falselist / nextlist rules"
  ]
 },
 "d5c77a1b552db740": {
  "sections": [
   [
    "Opportunities found",
    [
     {
      "table": {
       "head": [
        "Expression",
        "Observation",
        "Technique"
       ],
       "rows": [
        [
         "a + b (3 times), c + d (2 times)",
         "same operands, never reassigned in the loops",
         "Common subexpression elimination"
        ],
        [
         "(a+b) − (c+d), a*b, a+b−8 and their product",
         "do not depend on i or j",
         "Loop-invariant code motion — hoist out of both loops"
        ],
        [
         "Y[i]",
         "does not change in the j loop",
         "Hoist to the outer loop"
        ],
        [
         "i * 2",
         "invariant in the j loop",
         "Hoist to the outer loop"
        ],
        [
         "j * 2",
         "j is an induction variable",
         "Strength reduction: j2 = j2 + 2"
        ],
        [
         "P[i][j] and S[i][j]",
         "share (a+b) − (c+d)",
         "Reuse t3"
        ]
       ]
      }
     }
    ]
   ],
   [
    "Optimized code",
    [
     "t1 = a + b;\nt2 = c + d;\nt3 = t1 - t2;            // (a+b) - (c+d)\nt6 = (a * b) * (t1 - 8); // Q value\ni = 0;\nwhile (i < n) {\n    t7 = i * 2;          // invariant in the j loop\n    t8 = t3 + Y[i];      // S value for this row\n    j = 0; j2 = 0;       // j2 == 2*j\n    while (j < m) {\n        P[i][j] = t3;\n        Q[i][j] = t6;\n        R[i][j] = t7 - j2;\n        S[i][j] = t8;\n        j++; j2 = j2 + 2;\n    }\n    i++;\n}"
    ]
   ],
   [
    "Gain",
    [
     "Per inner iteration the original does 5 additions/subtractions on a, b, c, d, 3 multiplications and 2 subtractions for R; the optimized loop does one subtraction and one addition (j2). Work in the loop body drops from about 12 operations to 2."
    ]
   ]
  ],
  "sources": [
   "Compiler Design Module 5 notes, p. 137–144, 213–215 — principal sources of optimization"
  ]
 },
