 "683159af553a39e3": {
  "sections": [
   [
    "Three-address code",
    [
     "(1)  goto (14)\n(2)  if y > 10 goto (6)\n(3)  t1 = y - 5\n(4)  z = t1\n(5)  goto (17)\n(6)  t2 = y + 5\n(7)  z = t2\n(8)  goto (17)\n(9)  t3 = y * 2\n(10) z = t3\n(11) goto (17)\n(12) z = 0\n(13) goto (17)\n(14) if x == 1 goto (2)\n(15) if x == 2 goto (9)\n(16) goto (12)",
     "Translation scheme: code for each case body first, each ending in goto next (break); then the test block compares x with each case value and finally jumps to default."
    ]
   ]
  ],
  "sources": [
   "Compiler Design Module 4 notes, p. switch-case statements"
  ]
 },
 "ec77f943a4190fa6": {
  "sections": [
   [
    "Rules used",
    [
     {
      "table": {
       "head": [
        "Production",
        "Semantic action (backpatching)"
       ],
       "rows": [
        [
         "B → E1 relop E2",
         "B.truelist = makelist(nextinstr); B.falselist = makelist(nextinstr + 1); emit('if' E1 relop E2 'goto _'); emit('goto _')"
        ],
        [
         "B → B1 || M B2",
         "backpatch(B1.falselist, M.instr); B.truelist = merge(B1.truelist, B2.truelist); B.falselist = B2.falselist"
        ],
        [
         "B → B1 && M B2",
         "backpatch(B1.truelist, M.instr); B.truelist = B2.truelist; B.falselist = merge(B1.falselist, B2.falselist)"
        ],
        [
         "B → ! B1",
         "B.truelist = B1.falselist; B.falselist = B1.truelist"
        ],
        [
         "M → ε",
         "M.instr = nextinstr"
        ],
        [
         "N → ε",
         "N.nextlist = makelist(nextinstr); emit('goto _')"
        ],
        [
         "S → if (B) M S1",
         "backpatch(B.truelist, M.instr); S.nextlist = merge(B.falselist, S1.nextlist)"
        ],
        [
         "S → if (B) M1 S1 N else M2 S2",
         "backpatch(B.truelist, M1.instr); backpatch(B.falselist, M2.instr); S.nextlist = merge(S1.nextlist, N.nextlist, S2.nextlist)"
        ],
        [
         "S → while M1 (B) M2 S1",
         "backpatch(S1.nextlist, M1.instr); backpatch(B.truelist, M2.instr); S.nextlist = B.falselist; emit('goto' M1.instr)"
        ],
        [
         "L → L1 M S",
         "backpatch(L1.nextlist, M.instr); L.nextlist = S.nextlist"
        ]
       ]
      },
      "caption": "makelist(i) creates a list holding instruction i; merge joins lists; backpatch(p, i) writes i as the target of every jump in list p."
     }
    ]
   ],
   [
    "Steps",
    [
     {
      "table": {
       "head": [
        "Step",
        "Code / lists"
       ],
       "rows": [
        [
         "outer while: M1 = 100, B: a < 10",
         "100 if a<10 goto _ ; 101 goto _   t = {100}, f = {101}"
        ],
        [
         "M2 = 102 (body start)",
         "backpatch({100}, 102)"
        ],
        [
         "if: B: b == 0",
         "102, 103   t = {102}, f = {103}"
        ],
        [
         "then (M1 = 104): c := c + 1, then N",
         "backpatch({102}, 104); 104–105; 106 goto _  N.next = {106}"
        ],
        [
         "else (M2 = 107): inner while, B: d < 5",
         "backpatch({103}, 107); 107 if d<5 goto _ ; 108 goto _"
        ],
        [
         "inner body (M = 109): d := d + 1",
         "backpatch({107}, 109); 109–110; 111 goto 107; inner S.next = {108}"
        ],
        [
         "end of if-else",
         "if S.next = {106} ∪ {108}"
        ],
        [
         "end of outer while",
         "backpatch({106, 108}, 100); emit 112 goto 100; outer S.next = {101}"
        ],
        [
         "after the statement (next = 113)",
         "backpatch({101}, 113)"
        ]
       ]
      }
     }
    ]
   ],
   [
    "Final intermediate code",
    [
     "(100) if a < 10 goto (102)\n(101) goto (113)\n(102) if b == 0 goto (104)\n(103) goto (107)\n(104) t1 = c + 1\n(105) c = t1\n(106) goto (100)\n(107) if d < 5 goto (109)\n(108) goto (100)\n(109) t2 = d + 1\n(110) d = t2\n(111) goto (107)\n(112) goto (100)",
     "Instruction 112 is unreachable (both branches already jump back) but the scheme always emits it."
    ]
   ]
  ],
  "sources": [
   "Compiler Design Module 4 notes, p. backpatching section — truelist / falselist / nextlist rules"
  ]
 },
 "0694c874a86d8c6b": {
  "sections": [
   [
    "Principal sources of optimization in this program",
    [
     {
      "table": {
       "head": [
        "Statement",
        "Technique",
        "Result"
       ],
       "rows": [
        [
         "int unusedVar = x + 0;",
         "Algebraic simplification (x + 0 = x), then dead-code elimination (never used)",
         "removed"
        ],
        [
         "x = 5, y = 10 used everywhere",
         "Constant propagation",
         "x → 5, y → 10"
        ],
        [
         "if (x > 0 && y > 0)",
         "Constant folding: 5 > 0 && 10 > 0 = true",
         "test removed, body always runs"
        ],
        [
         "result = x*2 + y*2",
         "Folding (strength reduction x*2 → x+x is also possible)",
         "result = 30"
        ],
        [
         "result = 0 then result = 30",
         "Dead store elimination",
         "initial store removed"
        ],
        [
         "if (x < 0 || y < 0) result += 100",
         "Folding: false → unreachable code",
         "removed"
        ],
        [
         "printf(\"…\", result)",
         "Copy/constant propagation",
         "printf(\"Result = %d\\n\", 30)"
        ]
       ]
      }
     }
    ]
   ],
   [
    "Optimized code",
    [
     "int main() {\n    printf(\"Result = %d\\n\", 30);\n    return 0;\n}",
     "x, y and result become dead once their constant values are propagated, so their stores are removed as well."
    ]
   ]
  ],
  "sources": [
   "Compiler Design Module 5 notes, p. 137–144, 213–215 — principal sources of optimization"
  ]
 },
