 "61755c2640084c94": {
  "sections": [
   [
    "Left factoring",
    [
     "S → iEtSS′ | a | id := E — the alternatives start with i, a and id, all different ⇒ no factoring needed. S′ → eS | ε is fine.",
     "E → b | b+E | b*E | (E) — three alternatives share the prefix b:",
     "S  → i E t S S' | a | id := E\nS' → e S | ε\nE  → b E' | ( E )\nE' → + E | * E | ε"
    ]
   ],
   [
    "Recursive descent functions",
    [
     "void S() {\n    if (look == 'i')       { match('i'); E(); match('t'); S(); Sprime(); }\n    else if (look == 'a')  { match('a'); }\n    else if (look == ID)   { match(ID); match(ASSIGN); E(); }   /* id := E */\n    else error();\n}\nvoid Sprime() {\n    if (look == 'e') { match('e'); S(); }   /* else attaches to nearest if */\n    /* else ε */\n}\nvoid E() {\n    if (look == 'b')      { match('b'); Eprime(); }\n    else if (look == '(') { match('('); E(); match(')'); }\n    else error();\n}\nvoid Eprime() {\n    if (look == '+')      { match('+'); E(); }\n    else if (look == '*') { match('*'); E(); }\n    /* else ε */\n}",
     "Note: S′ → eS | ε still has the dangling-else choice (e ∈ FOLLOW(S′)); the code resolves it by taking e greedily."
    ]
   ]
  ],
  "sources": [
   "Compiler Design Module 2 notes, p. recursive-descent section — left recursion, left factoring, procedures"
  ]
 },
