 "57efcbd7fccbc6ed": {
  "sections": [
   [
    "Translation notes",
    [
     "The switch is translated as: evaluate the selector once (t1 = a + b), jump to the test block, emit each case body ending with goto next, and put the comparisons at test.",
     "Case 2 uses short-circuit code for (x != y) and (x >= y): if the first test fails, control goes straight to the else part.",
     "a[i][j] with a[40][40] and width 4: address = i × (40 × 4) + j × 4 = i × 160 + j × 4. (The loops run to 40, one past the last valid index, exactly as written.)"
    ]
   ],
   [
    "Three-address code",
    [
     "(1)  i = 0\n(2)  j = 0\n(3)  t1 = a + b\n(4)  goto (45)\n(5)  t2 = x + 1\n(6)  x = t2\n(7)  t3 = y + 2\n(8)  y = t3\n(9)  goto (49)\n(10) if x != y goto (12)\n(11) goto (21)\n(12) if x >= y goto (14)\n(13) goto (21)\n(14) t4 = a - 2\n(15) a = t4\n(16) t5 = b - 2\n(17) b = t5\n(18) t6 = c - 2\n(19) c = t6\n(20) goto (49)\n(21) t7 = a + 2\n(22) a = t7\n(23) t8 = b + 2\n(24) b = t8\n(25) t9 = c + 2\n(26) c = t9\n(27) goto (49)\n(28) i = 0\n(29) if i > 40 goto (49)\n(30) j = 0\n(31) if j > 40 goto (39)\n(32) t10 = i * 160\n(33) t11 = j * 4\n(34) t12 = t10 + t11\n(35) a[t12] = 0\n(36) t13 = j + 1\n(37) j = t13\n(38) goto (31)\n(39) t14 = i + 1\n(40) i = t14\n(41) goto (29)\n(42) t15 = a + b\n(43) a = t15\n(44) goto (49)\n(45) if t1 == 1 goto (5)\n(46) if t1 == 2 goto (10)\n(47) if t1 == 3 goto (28)\n(48) goto (42)"
    ]
   ]
  ],
  "sources": [
   "Compiler Design Module 4 notes, p. three-address code, quadruples, triples, indirect triples",
   "Compiler Design Module 4 notes, p. switch-case statements, translation of boolean expressions"
  ]
 },
