 "87b3cdedf78447c9": {
  "sections": [
   [
    "Short-circuit rule",
    [
     "A && B: if A is false the result is false and B is not evaluated.  A || B: if A is true the result is true and B is not evaluated."
    ]
   ],
   [
    "Semantic algorithm",
    [
     "eval(node):\n    case node of\n      id:      return value(id)\n      X && Y:  if eval(X) == false: return false      // skip Y\n               return eval(Y)\n      X || Y:  if eval(X) == true:  return true       // skip Y\n               return eval(Y)",
     "Equivalent jumping code (true/false exits):",
     "    if A goto L1\n    goto L2\nL1: if B goto Ltrue\n    goto L2\nL2: if C goto Ltrue\n    goto L3\nL3: if D goto Ltrue\n    goto Lfalse"
    ]
   ],
   [
    "Evaluation with A = true, B = false, C = true, D = false",
    [
     {
      "table": {
       "head": [
        "Step",
        "Evaluate",
        "Result",
        "Note"
       ],
       "rows": [
        [
         "1",
         "A",
         "true",
         "&& must look at B"
        ],
        [
         "2",
         "B",
         "false",
         "A && B = false"
        ],
        [
         "3",
         "C (left of inner ||)",
         "true",
         "C || D = true — D is NOT evaluated"
        ],
        [
         "4",
         "(A && B) || (C || D)",
         "true",
         "final"
        ]
       ]
      }
     },
     "E = true. Only A, B and C were evaluated."
    ]
   ]
  ],
  "sources": [
   "Compiler Design Module 4 notes, p. control-flow translation of boolean expressions"
  ]
 },
 "d6fdedded2d15e38": {
  "sections": [
   [
    "Rules",
    [
     {
      "table": {
       "head": [
        "Production",
        "Semantic action (backpatching)"
       ],
       "rows": [
        [
         "B → E1 relop E2",
         "B.truelist = makelist(nextinstr); B.falselist = makelist(nextinstr + 1); emit('if' E1 relop E2 'goto _'); emit('goto _')"
        ],
        [
         "B → B1 || M B2",
         "backpatch(B1.falselist, M.instr); B.truelist = merge(B1.truelist, B2.truelist); B.falselist = B2.falselist"
        ],
        [
         "B → B1 && M B2",
         "backpatch(B1.truelist, M.instr); B.truelist = B2.truelist; B.falselist = merge(B1.falselist, B2.falselist)"
        ],
        [
         "B → ! B1",
         "B.truelist = B1.falselist; B.falselist = B1.truelist"
        ],
        [
         "M → ε",
         "M.instr = nextinstr"
        ],
        [
         "N → ε",
         "N.nextlist = makelist(nextinstr); emit('goto _')"
        ],
        [
         "S → if (B) M S1",
         "backpatch(B.truelist, M.instr); S.nextlist = merge(B.falselist, S1.nextlist)"
        ],
        [
         "S → if (B) M1 S1 N else M2 S2",
         "backpatch(B.truelist, M1.instr); backpatch(B.falselist, M2.instr); S.nextlist = merge(S1.nextlist, N.nextlist, S2.nextlist)"
        ],
        [
         "S → while M1 (B) M2 S1",
         "backpatch(S1.nextlist, M1.instr); backpatch(B.truelist, M2.instr); S.nextlist = B.falselist; emit('goto' M1.instr)"
        ],
        [
         "L → L1 M S",
         "backpatch(L1.nextlist, M.instr); L.nextlist = S.nextlist"
        ]
       ]
      },
      "caption": "makelist(i) creates a list holding instruction i; merge joins lists; backpatch(p, i) writes i as the target of every jump in list p."
     }
    ]
   ],
   [
    "Code with lists (starting at 100)",
    [
     "100: if A > B goto 102\n101: goto _          // false\n102: if C < D goto _   // true\n103: goto 104\n104: if E != F goto _  // true\n105: goto _          // false",
     {
      "table": {
       "head": [
        "Step",
        "Lists"
       ],
       "rows": [
        [
         "A > B",
         "t = {100}, f = {101}"
        ],
        [
         "AND M (M = 102); C < D",
         "t = {102}, f = {103}"
        ],
        [
         "OR M (M = 104); E != F",
         "t = {104}, f = {105}"
        ],
        [
         "OR",
         "backpatch({103}, 104) ⇒ t = {102, 104}, f = {105}"
        ],
        [
         "AND",
         "backpatch({100}, 102) ⇒ B.t = {102, 104}, B.f = {101, 105}"
        ]
       ]
      }
     },
     "The remaining blanks are filled by the statement using the condition (true list → then-part, false list → else/exit)."
    ]
   ]
  ],
  "sources": [
   "Compiler Design Module 4 notes, p. backpatching section — truelist / falselist / nextlist rules"
  ]
 },
